### ============================================================
### Social Journal Backend — API Test Suite
### ============================================================
### Usage: Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension
### (Install: ritwickdey.rest-client)
### Set @baseUrl and credentials in the Variables section below
### ============================================================

### ── Variables ────────────────────────────────────────────────
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000
@email = demo@example.com
@password = SecurePass1!


### ============================================================
### 1. REGISTRATION
### ============================================================

### 1a. Register a new user (success)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "{{email}}",
    "username": "demouser",
    "first_name": "Demo",
    "last_name": "User",
    "password": "{{password}}",
    "password_confirm": "{{password}}"
}

###

### 1b. Register — weak password (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "weak@example.com",
    "username": "weakuser",
    "first_name": "Weak",
    "last_name": "User",
    "password": "weak",
    "password_confirm": "weak"
}

###

### 1c. Register — mismatched passwords (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "mismatch@example.com",
    "username": "mismatchuser",
    "first_name": "Mismatch",
    "last_name": "User",
    "password": "SecurePass1!",
    "password_confirm": "WrongPass1!"
}

###


### ============================================================
### 2. LOGIN
### ============================================================

### 2a. Login — valid credentials (sets httpOnly access + refresh cookies)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "identifier": "{{email}}",
    "password": "{{password}}"
}

###

### 2b. Login — invalid credentials (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "identifier": "{{email}}",
    "password": "wrongpassword"
}

###


### ============================================================
### 3. TOKEN REFRESH
### ============================================================

### 3a. Refresh auth cookies
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token/refresh/
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###


### ============================================================
### 4. USER PROFILE
### ============================================================

### 4a. Get current user profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/

###

### 4b. Update current user profile
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "first_name": "Updated",
    "last_name": "Name"
}

###

### 4c. Get profile — no token (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/

###


### ============================================================
### 5. MFA SETUP
### ============================================================

### 5a. Generate MFA secret and otpauth URI
### Copy the otpauth_uri into mfa_test.html to render the QR code
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/mfa/setup/

###

### 5b. MFA setup — no token (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/mfa/setup/

###


### ============================================================
### 6. MFA VERIFY
### ============================================================

### 6a. Verify TOTP code (replace 000000 with code from authenticator app)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/mfa/verify/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "totp_code": "481363"
}

###

### 6b. Verify — invalid code (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/mfa/verify/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "totp_code": "000000"
}

###

### 6c. Verify — no token (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/mfa/verify/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "totp_code": "000000"
}

###

### 6d. Verify — code too short (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/mfa/verify/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "totp_code": "123"
}

###


### ============================================================
### 7. LOGOUT
### ============================================================

### 7a. Logout — blacklists the refresh cookie (expect 205)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout/
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###

### 7b. Logout — attempt to use blacklisted refresh cookie (expect 401)
### Run this immediately after 7a to confirm blacklisting worked
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token/refresh/
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###

### 7c. Logout — no auth cookie (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout/
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###

### 7d. Logout — no auth token (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout/
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###

### ============================================================
### 8. CONTACTS
### ============================================================

### 8a. Create a contact
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "first_name": "John",
    "last_name": "Doe",
    "email": "john@example.com"
}

###

### 8b. List all contacts
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/

###

### 8c. Search contacts by name
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/?name=john

###

### 8d. Get single contact (replace 1 with real id)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/1/

###

### 8e. Update a contact
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/1/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "phone_number": "+15555550123"
}

###

### 8f. Add a fact
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/1/facts/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "detail_value": "Allergic to peanuts"
}

###

### 8g. List facts
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/1/facts/

###

### 8h. Add an observation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/1/observations/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "body": "Met at the coffee shop on Main St.",
    "is_active": true
}

###

### 8i. List observations
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/1/observations/

###

### 8j. Delete a contact
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/1/

###

### 8k. Access contact without token (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/
